  "source_shape_findings": [
    "Preserves connected B1+4F main building, broader left B1 polygon and lower1–3F mass, upper4F L-shaped occupied front row/right long wing and central3F low roof. Does not extrude the4F blank whole footprint to full height or interpret it as an all-floor courtyard.",
    "Common-core registration distinguishes B1/1F and2F–R page offsets. Source plan demonstrates the main tower, stepped wall rows and roof levels; no room partition claimed as measured facade window pattern. 2/3F hall blanks without void notation remain conservative solid interior proxies.",
    "4F left-front projection retains recessed lower floors and visible vertical support rather than a full rectangular block; roof separate stair inset is bounded as an existing core head approximation, not a new wing placed by its page position.",
    "787 front/main tower relative registration is consistent with the model-only comparison;786 shows main building behind a detached foreground monumental entrance, which is excluded together with neighboring red-brick buildings. These are not claimed as opposite facade photos.",
    "Right1F exterior stair revised from an over-simple straight flight to a source-footprint L-turn with connected treads. Entry landing, hillside contact and local base are bounded proxies, not surveyed grade or a whole campus landscape; necessary recessed spaces not indiscriminately filled.",
    "Tower-top folded/protruding multi-face source bay is coarsened to a rectangular projecting box. This remains an explicit geometric approximation, not exact facade reconstruction. Heights, slopes, window spacing/counts and colors are not measured; unknown rear details remain restrained rather than photo-mirrored.",
    "Six opaque material proxies use original Boolean run provenance, not nearest-face recoloring. No source photo/plan/PDF/overlay pixels, textures or source artwork are embedded. All five full-object views and three model-only source-angle comparisons personally inspected."
  ],
